&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager - Accounts, you will be responsible for the strategy, roadmap, and execution of Alpaca&#39;s core account management and identity verification systems. You will be the voice of our partners, working to create a flexible and compliant global account infrastructure. This role is critical to enabling financial institutions around the world to seamlessly and securely onboard and manage their end-users. You will work closely with engineering, legal, compliance, and business development teams to navigate the complexities of different jurisdictions and deliver a world-class account experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Things You Get To Do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the product vision, strategy, and roadmap for Alpaca&#39;s account opening and identity verification services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the lifecycle of various account structures, including fully disclosed, omnibus, and omnibus with sub-accounting, to meet the diverse needs of our global B2B clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and enhance features such as the ability to open accounts for entities, create sub-accounts for distinct trading strategies, and manage multiple account types (e.g., self-directed, robo, retirement)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the strategy for KYC and identity verification, supporting various models from partner-led KYC to integrated solutions with third-party providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with legal, compliance, and regional business teams to navigate the complexities of different jurisdictions, ensuring our account systems meet local licensing, data management, and financial requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author detailed product requirement documents (PRDs) and user stories to ensure clarity and alignment across all teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with go-to-market teams to enable adoption of new account features and onboarding flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and analyze key metrics such as onboarding success rates, account funding times, and KYC pass-through rates to measure success and identify areas for improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who You Are (Must-Haves):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of product management experience, with a focus on B2B, fintech, or complex platform products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with products related to user onboarding, identity verification (KYC/AML), or account management systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of the operational and regulatory complexities in financial services, especially concerning client onboarding and account lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to understand complex technical and business requirements and work effectively with engineering, legal, and compliance teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a proven track record of leading cross-functional teams and influencing stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven mindset with experience using analytics tools to track product performance and make informed decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine passion for financial markets and a strong desire to build products that empower developers and democratize access to financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in an agile development environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who You Might Be (Nice-to-Haves):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience working in the fintech or brokerage industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a globally distributed, remote-first company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with different brokerage account structures (e.g., omnibus, fully disclosed)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with global identity verification providers and regulatory technology (RegTech)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
